right hand figures shaking sometimes  

If your right hand (fingers) are shaking sometimes, it’s called a tremor. This can be harmless—or sometimes a sign of an underlying issue.

🔹 Common Causes (Most cases are not serious)
1. Stress / Anxiety 😟
When you're tense or nervous, hands may shake

Happens during pressure situations

2. Fatigue / Lack of Sleep 😴
Overworking or poor sleep can trigger shaking

3. Too Much Caffeine ☕
Coffee, tea, energy drinks can overstimulate nerves

4. Low Blood Sugar 🍬
Skipping meals → shakiness

Common in people with irregular eating habits

5. Muscle Fatigue 💪
After heavy work, gym, or repetitive hand use

🔹 Medical Conditions (if frequent)
6. Essential Tremor
Common neurological condition

Usually affects hands during movement

7. Parkinson’s disease
Tremor usually at rest

Often starts on one side (like right hand)

Slowness, stiffness also present

8. Thyroid Issues
Overactive thyroid can cause hand tremors

9. Vitamin Deficiency
Especially B12 deficiency

🔹 When to Worry ⚠️
See a doctor if:

Tremor is getting worse

Happens even at rest

You notice weakness, stiffness, or slow movement

It affects daily work (writing, eating)

🔹 What You Can Do Now
✔ Reduce caffeine
✔ Sleep 7–8 hours
✔ Eat regularly
✔ Manage stress (breathing, walking)
✔ Avoid alcohol/smoking

