cpus 2 meaning in aws 

In Amazon Web Services (AWS), when you see “2 CPUs”, it usually refers to:

🔹 👉 2 vCPUs (Virtual CPUs)
🔹 What is a vCPU?
A vCPU (virtual CPU) is a share of a physical processor core

AWS uses virtualization to divide real CPUs into multiple vCPUs

👉 So:

2 CPUs = 2 vCPUs

🔹 Simple Meaning
Your instance can handle 2 parallel processing tasks

Good for:

Small applications

Backend services

Dev/test environments

🔹 Example
If you launch an EC2 instance like:

t3.small → 2 vCPUs

t2.medium → 2 vCPUs

👉 It means:

The instance has 2 logical processing units

🔹 Real-World Analogy
1 vCPU = 1 worker

2 vCPUs = 2 workers doing tasks simultaneously

🔹 Important Note
vCPU ≠ physical CPU

Usually:

1 physical core = 2 vCPUs (hyper-threading)

🔹 When You Need More CPUs
Upgrade if:

High traffic apps

CPU usage > 70–80%

Slow performance

