how to write service to expose the nginx to access from browser

To access your NGINX pod from a browser in Kubernetes, you need to create a Service that exposes it.

🔹 Step 1: Make sure your Pod has a label
Your pod (or Deployment) must have labels so the Service can find it.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nginx-pod
  labels:
    app: nginx   # 👈 important
spec:
  containers:
  - name: nginx
    image: nginx:latest
    ports:
    - containerPort: 80
🔹 Step 2: Create a Service (NodePort)
This will expose NGINX so you can access it from your browser.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: nginx-service
spec:
  type: NodePort
  selector:
    app: nginx   # 👈 matches pod label
  ports:
  - protocol: TCP
    port: 80         # service port
    targetPort: 80   # container port
    nodePort: 30007  # external port (range: 30000–32767)
🔹 Step 3: Apply the files
kubectl apply -f pod.yml
kubectl apply -f service.yml
🔹 Step 4: Access in Browser 🌐
Find your node IP:

kubectl get nodes -o wide
Then open:

http://<Node-IP>:30007
👉 You should see the NGINX welcome page

🔹 Alternative (Easier for Testing)
If you're using local cluster (like Minikube):

minikube service nginx-service
🔹 Service Types (Quick Understanding)
Type	Use
ClusterIP	Internal only
NodePort	Access via IP:Port
LoadBalancer	Cloud external IP
🔹 Common Mistakes ❌
Label mismatch (selector != pod label)

Wrong port numbers

NodePort not in range (30000–32767)

