“Send traffic to all Pods that have label app: nginx”

🔹 How it works (Flow)
Pod has label:

labels:
  app: nginx
Service has selector:

selector:
  app: nginx
Kubernetes connects them:
👉 Service → finds matching Pods → sends traffic

🔹 What if NO label? ❌
Service cannot find your Pod

No traffic routing

Browser won’t work

🔹 Real-Life Analogy
Labels = Name tags on people

Service = Teacher calling students

👉 Teacher says: “All nginx students come here”

Only students with tag nginx will respond.

🔹 Important Concept
Labels are used by:

Services

Deployments

ReplicaSets

Network Policies

🔹 Example (Multiple Pods)
labels:
  app: nginx
  env: prod
You can even filter:

selector:
  app: nginx
  env: prod
🔹 Short Answer
👉 Label is required so Service can identify and connect to the correct Pod

